CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ by-copy capture snapshots the value at capture time: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[expr.prim.lambda.capture]: a by-copy capture is an unnamed non-static data
member of the closure object, direct-initialised from the entity at capture
time (a snapshot).  Lambda rework Phase B lowers an explicit-by-copy,
non-mutable, implicit-object lambda to a closure struct whose capture members
are initialised from the captured entities' values when the closure object is
created, so later modifications to the original variable are not observed.
